# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check the status {#check-the-status}"
msgstr "Den Status prüfen {#check-the-status}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Immediately after you call `run()`, the status is usually `QUEUED`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Unmittelbar nach dem Aufruf von `run()` ist der Status normalerweise `QUEUED`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Status | Meaning |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `QUEUED` | The job waits for a compute slot. |\n"
"| `INITIALIZING` | The workflow is starting an environment with the job's compute profile. |\n"
"| `RUNNING` | The workflow's entrypoint is running. |\n"
"| `RUNNING: <stage>` | The entrypoint reported a stage with [`update_status()`](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#report-progress-with-update_status), such as `RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU`. |\n"
"| `CANCELING` | You canceled the job, and the workflow is stopping it. |\n"
"| `DONE` | The entrypoint exited successfully. |\n"
"| `ERROR` | The entrypoint raised an error or exited with a nonzero code. See [Find the cause of an error](#find-the-cause-of-an-error). |\n"
"| `CANCELED` | You canceled the job, or it reached the [24-hour limit](#time-limit). |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Status | Bedeutung |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `QUEUED` | Der Job wartet auf einen Rechenplatz. |\n"
"| `INITIALIZING` | Der Workflow startet eine Umgebung mit dem Rechenprofil des Jobs. |\n"
"| `RUNNING` | Der Entrypoint des Workflows läuft. |\n"
"| `RUNNING: <stage>` | Der Entrypoint hat mit [`update_status()`](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#report-progress-with-update_status) eine Phase gemeldet, zum Beispiel `RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU`. |\n"
"| `CANCELING` | Du hast den Job abgebrochen, und der Workflow stoppt ihn gerade. |\n"
"| `DONE` | Der Entrypoint wurde erfolgreich beendet. |\n"
"| `ERROR` | Der Entrypoint hat einen Fehler ausgelöst oder wurde mit einem Exit-Code ungleich null beendet. Siehe [Die Ursache eines Fehlers finden](#find-the-cause-of-an-error). |\n"
"| `CANCELED` | Du hast den Job abgebrochen, oder er hat das [24-Stunden-Limit](#time-limit) erreicht. |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`DONE`, `ERROR`, and `CANCELED` are final, and `job.in_terminal_state()` returns `True` for them. A status loop that waits for another value, such as `SUCCEEDED`, never ends.\n"
msgstr "`DONE`, `ERROR` und `CANCELED` sind Endzustände, und `job.in_terminal_state()` gibt für sie `True` zurück. Eine Statusschleife, die auf einen anderen Wert wartet, etwa `SUCCEEDED`, endet nie.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Wait for the job to end {#wait-for-the-job-to-end}"
msgstr "Auf das Ende des Jobs warten {#wait-for-the-job-to-end}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To wait until the job ends, call `wait_for_final_state()`. It returns the final status, and with `verbose=True` it prints each status change. If you set `timeout` in seconds, `wait_for_final_state()` raises a `TimeoutError` when the time runs out before the job ends. The job keeps running:\n"
msgstr "Um zu warten, bis der Job endet, rufe `wait_for_final_state()` auf. Es gibt den endgültigen Status zurück, und mit `verbose=True` gibt es jede Statusänderung aus. Wenn du `timeout` in Sekunden festlegst, löst `wait_for_final_state()` einen `TimeoutError` aus, sobald die Zeit abläuft, bevor der Job endet. Der Job läuft weiter:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`wait_for_final_state()` checks the status after 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, and 32 seconds, and then every 60 seconds, so it sees the end of a short job within seconds and makes few requests for a long job. To check at a fixed interval instead, pass `poll_interval` in seconds.\n"
msgstr "`wait_for_final_state()` prüft den Status nach 1, 2, 4, 8, 16 und 32 Sekunden und danach alle 60 Sekunden. So erkennt es das Ende eines kurzen Jobs innerhalb von Sekunden und stellt bei einem langen Job nur wenige Anfragen. Um stattdessen in einem festen Intervall zu prüfen, übergib `poll_interval` in Sekunden.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read the logs {#read-the-logs}"
msgstr "Die Logs lesen {#read-the-logs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Anything that the workflow writes to standard output or standard error goes to the job's logs. You can read them with `job.logs()` while the job runs, before it has a result:\n"
msgstr "Alles, was der Workflow in die Standardausgabe oder in die Standardfehlerausgabe schreibt, landet in den Logs des Jobs. Du kannst sie mit `job.logs()` lesen, während der Job läuft, noch bevor er ein Ergebnis hat:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The workflow uploads new log lines about every 15 seconds, and one last time when the job ends or is canceled. Immediately after a job starts, `job.logs()` returns `No logs yet.`\n"
msgstr "Der Workflow lädt neue Logzeilen etwa alle 15 Sekunden hoch und ein letztes Mal, wenn der Job endet oder abgebrochen wird. Unmittelbar nach dem Start eines Jobs gibt `job.logs()` `No logs yet.` zurück.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The workflow keeps the newest 50 MB of logs for each job, and adds a line at the top that says the logs were truncated.\n"
msgstr "Der Workflow behält für jeden Job die neuesten 50 MB an Logs und fügt oben eine Zeile hinzu, die besagt, dass die Logs gekürzt wurden.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To decide what your workflow logs, see [Write logs](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#write-logs). To show only the lines that match a regular expression, pass `include` to `job.filtered_logs()`. To hide lines, pass `exclude`.\n"
msgstr "Was dein Workflow protokolliert, legst du wie unter [Logs schreiben](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#write-logs) beschrieben fest. Um nur die Zeilen anzuzeigen, die zu einem regulären Ausdruck passen, übergib `include` an `job.filtered_logs()`. Um Zeilen auszublenden, übergib `exclude`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Get the result {#get-the-result}"
msgstr "Das Ergebnis abrufen {#get-the-result}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`job.result()` waits until the job ends, then returns the value that the workflow passed to [`save_result()`](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#save-results):\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"`job.result()` wartet, bis der Job endet, und gibt dann den Wert zurück, den der Workflow an [`save_result()`](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#save-results) übergeben hat:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By default, `job.result()` checks the status every 30 seconds and waits with no time limit. Pass `maxwait` to limit the number of checks. For example, `job.result(maxwait=40)` waits about 20 minutes. To check one time without waiting, pass `wait=False`. If `job.result()` stops waiting before the job ends, it returns `{}`.\n"
msgstr "Standardmäßig prüft `job.result()` den Status alle 30 Sekunden und wartet ohne Zeitlimit. Übergib `maxwait`, um die Anzahl der Prüfungen zu begrenzen. Zum Beispiel wartet `job.result(maxwait=40)` etwa 20 Minuten. Um einmal zu prüfen, ohne zu warten, übergib `wait=False`. Wenn `job.result()` zu warten aufhört, bevor der Job endet, gibt es `{}` zurück.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check how long each stage took {#check-how-long-each-stage-took}"
msgstr "Prüfen, wie lange jede Phase gedauert hat {#check-how-long-each-stage-took}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`job.events()` lists every status and stage change of a job with its time, so you can see how long the job waited for compute and how long each stage took:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"`job.events()` listet jede Status- und Phasenänderung eines Jobs mit ihrer Zeit auf, sodass du sehen kannst, wie lange der Job auf Rechenleistung gewartet hat und wie lange jede Phase dauerte:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The events use the stored status names. `PENDING` is `INITIALIZING`, and `SUCCEEDED` is `DONE`. For the QPU usage of a run, see [Find the QPU jobs of a run](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#find-the-qpu-jobs-of-a-run).\n"
msgstr "Die Ereignisse verwenden die gespeicherten Statusnamen. `PENDING` entspricht `INITIALIZING`, und `SUCCEEDED` entspricht `DONE`. Zur QPU-Nutzung eines Laufs siehe [Die QPU-Jobs eines Laufs finden](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#find-the-qpu-jobs-of-a-run).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Find the cause of an error {#find-the-cause-of-an-error}"
msgstr "Die Ursache eines Fehlers finden {#find-the-cause-of-an-error}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When the workflow raises an exception, the job ends with the `ERROR` status. For example, run the workflow with an angle that it rejects:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Wenn der Workflow eine Exception auslöst, endet der Job mit dem Status `ERROR`. Führe den Workflow zum Beispiel mit einem Winkel aus, den er ablehnt:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The logs show the traceback:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Die Logs zeigen den Traceback:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`job.result()` raises a `QiskitServerlessException`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"`job.result()` raises a `QiskitServerlessException`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the workflow [reports errors with `send_error()`](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error), read them with `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")`, and read their messages with `job.error_message()`. For a job without reported errors, `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` returns an empty list, and `job.error_message()` returns `{}`.\n"
msgstr "Wenn der Workflow [Fehler mit `send_error()` meldet](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#best-practice-report-errors-with-send_error), lies sie mit `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` und ihre Meldungen mit `job.error_message()`. Bei einem Job ohne gemeldete Fehler gibt `job.events(type=\"ERROR\")` eine leere Liste zurück, und `job.error_message()` gibt `{}` zurück.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: for custom workflows on Fleets, a raised ServerlessError is not recorded as an error event: only provider jobs run inside gateway/templates/main.tmpl, which calls send_error(). Custom jobs run the entrypoint directly through fleet_custom_job_wrapper.py. Confirm whether custom jobs should get the same handler, and whether error_message() should return a string instead of {}. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Manage jobs {#manage-jobs}"
msgstr "Jobs verwalten {#manage-jobs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cancel a job {#cancel-a-job}"
msgstr "Einen Job abbrechen {#cancel-a-job}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Cancel a job with `job.cancel()`. The status changes to `CANCELING` while the workflow stops the job, and then to `CANCELED`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Breche einen Job mit `job.cancel()` ab. Der Status wechselt zu `CANCELING`, während der Workflow den Job stoppt, und danach zu `CANCELED`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.cancel()` returns a message about the job and about its [linked QPU jobs](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs), which it also tries to cancel. For a running job, the workflow sends `SIGTERM` to your entrypoint. To save partial results, see [Clean up when a job is canceled](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled). If the job already ended, `job.cancel()` returns `Job already in terminal state.` and changes nothing.\n"
msgstr "`job.cancel()` gibt eine Meldung über den Job und über seine [verknüpften QPU-Jobs](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#cancel-linked-qpu-jobs) zurück, die es ebenfalls abzubrechen versucht. Bei einem laufenden Job sendet der Workflow `SIGTERM` an deinen Entrypoint. Wie du Teilergebnisse speicherst, siehe [Aufräumen, wenn ein Job abgebrochen wird](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled). Wenn der Job bereits beendet ist, gibt `job.cancel()` `Job already in terminal state.` zurück und ändert nichts.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: in a live test (1 Nov 2026), a job canceled while RUNNING went to CANCELING and then DONE, with its result saved, because the entrypoint finished before the stop took effect. Confirm whether a job that finishes during CANCELING should end as DONE or CANCELED. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Find a job from a new session {#find-a-job-from-a-new-session}"
msgstr "Einen Job aus einer neuen Session wiederfinden {#find-a-job-from-a-new-session}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `Job` object and the workflow exist only in your current Python session. After you restart a notebook kernel, pass the saved job ID to `client.job()`, or list your recent jobs with `client.jobs()`:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"
msgstr ""
"Das `Job`-Objekt und der Workflow existieren nur in deiner aktuellen Python-Session. Nachdem du einen Notebook-Kernel neu gestartet hast, übergib die gespeicherte Job-ID an `client.job()` oder liste deine letzten Jobs mit `client.jobs()` auf:\n"
"**`run_workflow_remotely.ipynb`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`client.jobs()` returns your 10 most recent jobs, newest first. Filter it with `function`, `status` (from the [status table](#check-the-status)), or `created_after` (an ISO 8601 timestamp), and page through it with `limit` and `offset`. To list the workflows that you uploaded, call `client.list()`.\n"
msgstr "`client.jobs()` gibt deine 10 neuesten Jobs zurück, den neuesten zuerst. Filtere mit `function`, `status` (aus der [Statustabelle](#check-the-status)) oder `created_after` (ein ISO-8601-Zeitstempel) und blättere mit `limit` und `offset` durch die Liste. Um die Workflows aufzulisten, die du hochgeladen hast, rufe `client.list()` auf.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [Workloads](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads) table on IBM Quantum Platform also lists your jobs, with their status, compute profile, and run times.\n"
msgstr "Die Tabelle [Workloads](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads) auf IBM Quantum Platform listet ebenfalls deine Jobs auf, mit ihrem Status, Rechenprofil und ihren Laufzeiten.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Time limit {#time-limit}"
msgstr "Zeitlimit {#time-limit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A managed workflow cancels a job that runs for more than 24 hours, and the job ends with the `CANCELED` status. During long runs, [save checkpoints to file storage](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs) so that you do not lose work.\n"
msgstr "Ein verwalteter Workflow bricht einen Job ab, der länger als 24 Stunden läuft, und der Job endet mit dem Status `CANCELED`. Bei langen Läufen [speichere Checkpoints im Dateispeicher](/guides/manage-files-across-managed-workflows#best-practice-checkpoint-long-jobs), damit du keine Arbeit verlierst.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: the timeout is measured from the job's latest event, not from its start (gateway/scheduler/tasks/update_fleets_jobs_statuses.py stop_job_if_timeout). Calls to update_status() and send_error() create events, so a job that reports stages can run longer than 24 hours. This looks like a bug; confirm the intended behavior. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troubleshoot jobs {#troubleshoot-jobs}"
msgstr "Probleme bei Jobs beheben {#troubleshoot-jobs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Problem | Cause |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `run()` fails with `Code: 429` and `Active job limit reached.` | You reached the [active job limit](/guides/run-parameter-sweep#active-job-limit). Wait for some jobs to end, or [cancel](#cancel-a-job) jobs that you no longer need. |\n"
"| The job stays `QUEUED`, and `run()` warned that `your account, plan or subscription is blocked`. | The job does not start until the block on your account, plan, or subscription is lifted. Contact your administrator. |\n"
"| `job.logs()` returns `No logs yet.` | The job is queued or just started. Wait about 15 seconds. |\n"
"| `job.result()` returns `{}` | The job has not ended, was canceled, or saved no result. See [Save results](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#save-results). |\n"
"| `job.error_message()` returns `{}` | The workflow raised an exception without reporting an error. Read the traceback with `job.logs()`. |\n"
"| The job is `CANCELED`, but you did not cancel it | The job reached the [24-hour limit](#time-limit). |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Problem | Ursache |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `run()` schlägt mit `Code: 429` und `Active job limit reached.` fehl. | Du hast das [Limit für aktive Jobs](/guides/run-parameter-sweep#active-job-limit) erreicht. Warte, bis einige Jobs enden, oder [breche](#cancel-a-job) Jobs ab, die du nicht mehr brauchst. |\n"
"| Der Job bleibt `QUEUED`, und `run()` hat gewarnt: `your account, plan or subscription is blocked`. | Der Job startet erst, wenn die Sperre deines Kontos, Plans oder Abonnements aufgehoben ist. Wende dich an deine Administratorin oder deinen Administrator. |\n"
"| `job.logs()` gibt `No logs yet.` zurück. | Der Job steht in der Warteschlange oder wurde gerade gestartet. Warte etwa 15 Sekunden. |\n"
"| `job.result()` gibt `{}` zurück. | Der Job ist nicht beendet, wurde abgebrochen oder hat kein Ergebnis gespeichert. Siehe [Ergebnisse speichern](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs#save-results). |\n"
"| `job.error_message()` gibt `{}` zurück. | Der Workflow hat eine Exception ausgelöst, ohne einen Fehler zu melden. Lies den Traceback mit `job.logs()`. |\n"
"| Der Job ist `CANCELED`, aber du hast ihn nicht abgebrochen. | Der Job hat das [24-Stunden-Limit](#time-limit) erreicht. |\n"

